name o5-04-no-radar-1
timeout 700
time 1999-03-24T21:00:00Z

# CAMPAIGN O5, SORTIE 4 OF 10 - AIRFIELD DEFENCE: BATAJNICA, 24-26 MARCH 1999.
# THE RADAR, SWITCHED OFF - THE ANCHOR'S OWN SERVICEABILITY, ISOLATED.
# Spec, anchor and sources: doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md. Format: doc/missions/campaign.md.
# CONTROL: o5-01-cap.fbm - identical but for the two `set n019_mode` lines.
#
# THE ARENA, and every coordinate in it is [SET]. Batajnica lies at ~44.93 N 20.26 E [T4, approximate -
# doc/campaigns/o5-airfield-defence.md says so and this campaign does not improve on it]. FlightBox flies
# it under `--elev const` on a 0 m datum (the real field is ~80 m) and with NO TERRAIN MASKING (gap C4),
# so the Fruska Gora, the Danube valley and every mask a Serbian battery used do not exist here. The
# field's runway heading (110 deg) and length (3 000 m) are [SET]; nothing in this campaign lands.
#   the field       44.93000 20.26000, with the fuel farm, a hangar row, one hardened shelter and the
#                   runway aim point around it
#   the point defence  P-18 node at 20.24000 (on the field), S-125 at 20.16000 (7.9 km W), 2K12 at
#                   20.19000/44.95500 (5.7 km W, 2.8 km N), ZSU-23-4 at 20.25200 (0.7 km W)
#   the package     ingresses due east along 44.93 N from 19.60000 (52.0 km out) at 5 000 m and 450 kt
# Scale at this latitude: 1 deg of longitude = 78 800 m, 1 deg of latitude = 111 132 m [DERIVED].
#
# THE SUBSTITUTION, AND ITS DIRECTION. The package that attacked Batajnica was F-15C, F-117 and cruise
# missiles [T4]; FlightBox flies F-16s for all three, which is declared and not hidden. THE F-15C ROW
# EXISTS AND IS DELIBERATELY NOT USED, and the reason was MEASURED in this round rather than assumed:
# `modules/air/FBAirModule` composes NO FIRE CONTROL, so `FBState::FireControl` is never written and all
# three of FBPilot's weapon-employment gates stay shut. Measured: an `f15c` with four AIM-120 designates
# at t = 8.6 s at 18.64 nm, holds `eng_locked = 1` for 28 s from 18.6 down to 8.8 nm, and never posts a
# WeaponRelease. A catalogue row is ACCEPTED as a FLIGHT MODEL, not as a combatant.
# The defender is the MiG-29 the 127th "Knights" actually flew - so unlike O1 and O3 the substitution
# here is on the ATTACKER's side, and it makes the attacker WEAKER than history (no F-117, no cruise
# missile, no AIM-7/AMRAAM mix from a 160 km radar). A FlightBox Batajnica in which the field still
# loses says something WEAKER than 1999 did, not stronger.
#
# THE TWO LAYERS CANNOT BOTH BE LIVE, AND IT IS THIS CAMPAIGN'S STRUCTURAL DISCLOSURE - stated in every
# file because a reader who skips it will read every result backwards.
#   1. A FlightBox SAM site has NO IFF INTERROGATOR (`modules/ground/FBSiteModule`: "a battery has no
#      IFF interrogator in this tree") and an FBRadarContact carries no identity by construction, so a
#      battery engages the NEAREST FIRM TRACK in its envelope whoever it belongs to. An AIRFIELD is
#      exactly the geometry in which the friendly aircraft are the nearest track: O1 could lay its CAP
#      outside its own umbrella, O5 cannot, because the defenders live under it.
#   2. `missions/FBMissionRunner` ENDS THE WHOLE RUN at the first flight-monitor K.O. (`FirstFlightKo`),
#      and a mission-killed F-16 falls from 5 000 m in about 122 s. So an air engagement and a bomb run
#      in one file are not two measurements, they are one measurement and a truncation.
# The answer taken is the one a real airfield takes and the only one this format can express: the
# missiles are HELD while the fighters are up (`set emcon hold <offS> <onS>`, the briefed emission plan
# of round C26) and free when they are not. Sorties 01-05 therefore measure the FIGHTER layer with the
# belt briefed quiet; 06-07 measure the MISSILE layer with no fighter airborne; the chain 08-10 lets the
# campaign's own attrition decide which layer is left. THE CAMPAIGN NEVER MEASURES BOTH AT ONCE, and any
# claim that it did would be manufactured.
#
# THE ONE TACTICAL QUESTION: WHAT IS A RADARLESS MiG-29 WORTH? `set n019_mode rad` becomes
# `set n019_mode off` on both aircraft and nothing else changes. This is the Batajnica condition
# isolated: the anchor says the serviceable aircraft flew with "outdated avionics, degraded radar
# performance and a limited stock of R-73/R-27" [T4], and the radar is the half of that FlightBox can
# declare exactly.
#
# WHAT THE AIRCRAFT STILL HAS, AND WHAT USES IT. It keeps the KOLS infrared search, the SPO-15 and a gun.
# THE PILOT USES NONE OF THE FIRST: `doc/duels.md` D3 - the intercept picture is built from the Radar
# block alone, so a passive sensor cues nothing. This sortie is therefore expected to measure ZERO, and
# the zero is the point: it prices the gap rather than hiding it. The controller is still briefed, so the
# aircraft is pointed correctly at a raid it cannot see - "confidently blind" in the other channel.
#
# MEASURED (fingerprint ee634cab56b128ce): ZERO, AND THE ZERO IS THE POINT. No radar contact, no shot,
# and `irst_contacts` = 0 for the whole 700 s - the KOLS never had anything to offer on this geometry and
# nothing would have read it if it had. Both strikers release; `m4sa3` and `m4nod` are destroyed. The
# pair flies its briefed vector correctly the whole time, so this is not a navigation failure: A
# RADARLESS MiG-29 IS NOT A DEGRADED INTERCEPTOR IN THIS TREE, IT IS AN ABSENT ONE. That prices the
# anchor's serviceability sentence exactly, and it prices gap D3 at the whole sortie.
#
# READING RULE: exit 3 expected. Read `radar RADAR_CONTACT` (expected: none), `irst_contacts` in the
# telemetry (whether the KOLS had something the pilot never asked for), `sms RELEASE ... store=r27r`
# (expected: none) and the mk84 count. A run in which the pair engages anyway would mean the radar switch
# does not reach the fire control and would be a defect.

zone umbrella 44.93000 20.16000 35000 100 18000   # the S-125's published envelope, as geometry
zone field    44.93000 20.26000  6000   0  6000   # the terminal box: first entry is the time-on-target

net batajnica
  control m4nod
  link radio 60000 mast 8
  period 4.0
  hold 3
  wcs free
  member m4nod
  member m4sa3 autonomy hold
  member m4sa6 autonomy hold
  member m4flk autonomy hold

unit m4kna
  team hostile
  flight kn1 1
  module mig29
  spawn 44.93000 20.35000 9000 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode off
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 50 5
  set brief_gci 60 270 31 5
  set brief_gci 100 270 13 5
  wp 44.93000 19.40000 9000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective deny release team friendly
  objective survive

unit m4knb
  team hostile
  flight kn1 2
  module mig29
  spawn 44.94500 20.35000 9150 270.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 60
  set n019_mode off
  set n019_range_nm 27
  set n019_emission illum
  set rwr on
  set brief_sort left
  set store 3 r27r
  set store 4 r27r
  set store 5 r73
  set store 6 r73
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 30
  set cmds_flare 30
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task intercept
  set brief_gci 20 270 50 5
  set brief_gci 60 270 31 5
  set brief_gci 100 270 13 5
  wp 44.93000 19.40000 9000 450
  objective kill team friendly
  objective deny release team friendly
  objective survive

unit m4stra
  team friendly
  flight st1 1
  module f16
  spawn 44.93000 19.60000 5000 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.93000 20.16000 5000 450
  objective kill unit m4sa3
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m4strb
  team friendly
  flight st1 2
  module f16
  spawn 44.94500 19.60000 5150 90.0 450
  set gear up
  set fuel_pct 80
  set datalink on
  set fcr_mode off
  set rwr on
  set store 3 mk84
  set store 7 mk84
  set cmds_mode man
  set cmds_program 1
  set cmds_chaff 60
  set cmds_flare 60
  set brief_master_arm arm
  set task attack
  set attack_mode ccrp
  wp 44.94000 20.24000 5150 450
  objective kill unit m4nod
  objective avoid zone umbrella

unit m4nod
  module p18
  team hostile
  spawn 44.94000 20.24000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon free

unit m4sa3
  module sa3
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93000 20.16000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold 1 3600
  set rounds 4

unit m4sa6
  module sa6
  team hostile
  spawn 44.95500 20.19000 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold 1 3600
  set rounds 3

unit m4flk
  module zsu23
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93300 20.25200 ground 0.0 0
  set emcon hold 1 3600
  objective no_fire
  objective survive

unit m4ful
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93800 20.25000 ground 0.0 0

unit m4hgr
  module target_soft
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93200 20.23500 ground 0.0 0

unit m4has
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 44.93500 20.27000 ground 0.0 0

unit m4rwy
  module target_hard
  team hostile
  spawn 44.92700 20.27500 ground 0.0 0
